# Multi-agent worktrees
.worktrees/
.claude/worktrees/

# Finder / file-sync duplicates. A sync client on at least one dev machine creates
# "name 2.ts" copies of every file during a large checkout.
#
# They do NOT reach vitest: its glob is `src/**/*.test.ts`, and `week.test 2.ts` does not
# match it. What they reach is everything that walks the tree itself — `tsc`'s
# `include: ["src/**/*.ts"]`, the dead-code audits, `boundaries.test.ts`, `derive.test.ts`,
# `documentation.test.ts`. On 2026-07-31 a polluted tree produced 21 failures with nothing
# wrong in the code, and `dist/` copies made `process.test.ts` spawn a stale CLI for 5 more.
#
# Deleting them needs -x. These patterns make the files *ignored*, and `git clean` skips
# ignored files unless told otherwise, so the obvious `git clean -f '* 2.*'` is a silent
# no-op — it reports nothing and removes nothing. Preview, then delete:
#
#   git clean -nxd '* 2.*' '* 2'
#   git clean -fxd '* 2.*' '* 2'
#
# `npm run review` fails when any are present, so CI says so before a confusing red suite does.
* 2.*
* 2

# Scratch harnesses — the first line of defence, and deliberately not the only one.
#
# The repository's convention is that a measurement harness is written, run, and deleted before the
# commit. `measure-tmp.mjs` was committed anyway in `8d6d811`, carrying the header
# `/* … Scratch file; not committed. */` and a `/home/user/...` worktree path from another machine,
# so it could not run anywhere and nothing referenced it. It sat in the tree for a fortnight.
#
# These patterns would have caught that one at `git add -A`, which is `RISKS.md` R25's exact
# mechanism. They are **not** the guard, because a pattern is silent by construction: it does not
# fail, `git add -f` walks past it, and it has no effect on a file that is already tracked. The
# guard is `packages/experiments/src/validation/scratchFiles.test.ts`, which reads the tracked set
# and goes red. This is the cheap half that stops the common case before it needs the loud half.
*-tmp.mjs
*-tmp.js
*.scratch.*
/scratch/
probe-*.mjs
scrollprobe*.mjs
